-- DUMBWAITER (ruled 2026-09-21): a right single quotation mark (’, U+2019)
-- pasted in from Word/Pages/Google Docs, standing in for the plain `'s`
-- genitive dereference. The lexer grammar itself stays strict -- `TGenitive`
-- has no payload and always exactprints as `'s`, so teaching it to also
-- accept the curly spelling would break the `exactprint identity` law --
-- so this fails to lex, with a diagnostic naming the glyph and the fix
-- rather than megaparsec's raw "unexpected" dump.
--
-- See doc/reference/errors/README.md, "Curly quotes and dashes from a word
-- processor".

DECLARE Person
  HAS age IS A NUMBER

GIVEN p IS A Person
DECIDE `is adult` IF p’s age >= 18
